| Topic | Link |
|-------|------|
| Next.js Docs | https://nextjs.org/docs |
| Tailwind CSS Docs | https://tailwindcss.com/docs |
| Stripe Checkout | https://stripe.com/docs/payments/checkout |
| Auth0 Quickstart | https://auth0.com/docs/quickstart/spa/react |
| Cypress Guide | https://docs.cypress.io/guides/overview/why-cypress |
| SEO for SPA | https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/seo-basics |

---

### TL;DR

1. **Plan** → Wireframe → Prototype.  
2. **Stack**: React + Next.js + Redux Toolkit + Tailwind CSS.  
3. **Folder**: `pages/`, `components/`, `store/`, `services/`.  
4. **Core pages**: Home, Products, Product Detail, Cart, Checkout, Account.  
5. **API**: Axios wrapper, serverless functions for checkout.  
6. **Auth**: Auth0 or Firebase.  
7. **Payment**: Stripe Checkout.  
8. **Test**: Jest + Cypress.  
9. **Deploy**: Vercel + GitHub Actions.  

Follow this roadmap, tweak the tech choices to fit your team’s expertise, and you’ll have a scalable, SEO‑friendly e‑commerce frontend in no time. Happy coding! 🚀
